  "description": "#EXP-1674 (L2): THE `#IDENT` scan ×4: web lib/issue-refs.ts (`splitIssueRefs`), desktop markdown/editor.rs (`scan_issue_refs_with`), iOS ExpUI IssueRefs.swift (`IssueRefs.matches`), Android ui/markdown/IssueRefs.kt (`IssueRefs.findAll`). Interchange form: `#` not glued to an ASCII word character or another `#`, then `{PREFIX}-{number}` (a letter, letters or digits, `-`, digits; any case), ending at a boundary (no ASCII word character or `-` after it). Bare mode (agent narration only, display-only, never stored): also an identifier with no `#`, whose prefix is UPPERCASE, not glued to an ASCII word character, `#` or `-`; `/` before it is fine. Word characters and digits are ASCII ONLY on every client: a non-ASCII character next to a token is a boundary, a non-ASCII digit is no digit. `hash` = the tokens as written in the default mode, `bare` = in bare mode, left to right; the `#` is part of a token written with one. Code spans are the caller's concern, so none here. Only a token that RESOLVES becomes tappable; the rest stays text.",
